WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.120
- Give it up for Donnie, Joey,

00:00:02.120 --> 00:00:04.392
Jordan, Jonathan, and Danny, y'all!

00:00:04.392 --> 00:00:07.391
(audience cheers)

00:00:07.391 --> 00:00:09.940
I know that most people
here probably know this,

00:00:09.940 --> 00:00:10.773
most people in the planet,

00:00:10.773 --> 00:00:12.520
but how did y'all first get together?

00:00:12.520 --> 00:00:14.090
'Cause I actually don't know that story.

00:00:14.090 --> 00:00:14.923
- Oh my gosh, okay.

00:00:14.923 --> 00:00:17.380
We grew up in Boston, Massachusetts,

00:00:17.380 --> 00:00:18.861
home of New Edition.

00:00:18.861 --> 00:00:21.070
- [Kelly] Yes!
(audience cheers)

00:00:21.070 --> 00:00:22.640
- Most of us were bused to school

00:00:22.640 --> 00:00:25.920
literally two blocks away
from where they grew up.

00:00:25.920 --> 00:00:27.130
And while they were famous, you know,

00:00:27.130 --> 00:00:30.610
it was a really amazing
time to be a fan of theirs.

00:00:30.610 --> 00:00:32.380
Their producer, Maurice Starr,

00:00:32.380 --> 00:00:34.870
wanted to get another band together,

00:00:34.870 --> 00:00:35.703
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:00:35.703 --> 00:00:38.550
- after them, and
started to look for kids.

00:00:38.550 --> 00:00:40.190
Now, the story is that there was

00:00:40.190 --> 00:00:42.560
thousands of auditions, kind
of like an American Idol thing.

00:00:42.560 --> 00:00:43.393
- Yeah.
- It wasn't that.

00:00:43.393 --> 00:00:45.390
There was about seven people auditioned.

00:00:45.390 --> 00:00:47.693
Thank God, because we probably
wouldn't have made it,

00:00:47.693 --> 00:00:48.526
(participants and audience laugh)

00:00:48.526 --> 00:00:49.979
if we have to go through
what you went through.

00:00:49.979 --> 00:00:50.812
- It's a big difference.

00:00:50.812 --> 00:00:51.645
- Yeah, it's a big difference.

00:00:51.645 --> 00:00:52.710
But we were the guys.

00:00:52.710 --> 00:00:55.520
I was the first member that met Maurice.

00:00:55.520 --> 00:00:56.441
My brother Mark actually

00:00:56.441 --> 00:00:58.560
was one of the first members with me,

00:00:58.560 --> 00:01:00.618
but he couldn't sing.

00:01:00.618 --> 00:01:02.660
(everyone laughs)

00:01:02.660 --> 00:01:03.493
- He's doing poorly.
- I can't either,

00:01:03.493 --> 00:01:06.420
but he was worse.
- He's doing poorly (laughs).

00:01:06.420 --> 00:01:10.724
So, I was friends with
Danny, Jonathan and Jordan.

00:01:10.724 --> 00:01:14.140
Over time I talked them into
coming and meeting Maurice,

00:01:14.140 --> 00:01:15.360
and they decided to join.

00:01:15.360 --> 00:01:17.867
Then we needed the special ingredient.

00:01:17.867 --> 00:01:19.915
- [Joey] Ah, ha ha ha!
- [Kelly] The special sauce.

00:01:19.915 --> 00:01:20.748
- [Donnie] And Joey had-

00:01:20.748 --> 00:01:21.581
- [Joey] The little little guy.

00:01:21.581 --> 00:01:23.660
- He built the reputation
for himself around the city

00:01:23.660 --> 00:01:24.860
doing plays and stuff.

00:01:24.860 --> 00:01:26.540
Maurice kept saying, we need that young

00:01:26.540 --> 00:01:28.380
Donny Osmond/Michael Jackson type of guy

00:01:28.380 --> 00:01:29.270
in the front of the band,

00:01:29.270 --> 00:01:31.920
and we found Joey and the rest is history.

00:01:31.920 --> 00:01:33.064
(audience cheers)
- [Kelly] It's so interesting

00:01:33.064 --> 00:01:34.703
how it all plays out.

